files-apply-hint = The declaration is saved but not placed in any sandbox yet. Place the declared files in every registered project with:
warning-file-looks-like-credential = { $source } has a name that often holds credentials.
files-pull-same = The sandbox copy of { $destination } in { $project } already matches { $source }.
files-pull-diff = The sandbox copy of { $destination } in { $project } differs from { $source }:
files-pull-adopted = Adopted the sandbox copy of { $destination } from { $project } into { $source }.
files-pull-spread-hint = The other projects still hold the previous version. Place it in every registered project with:
files-pull-kept = Kept { $source } as it was. The copy in { $project } is left as it is.
files-pull-undecided = Nothing was adopted. Run the command in an interactive terminal to choose whether to adopt the sandbox copy.
save-done = Saved the commits of { $project } into { $repository } under refs/sbx/{ $namespace }.
save-unchanged = { $repository } already holds every commit of { $project }.
save-nothing = { $project } has no branch or tag to save yet.
save-branches-untouched = Your branches and tags in the host repository were left as they were. A tip that was replaced or deleted is kept under archive and is never removed automatically.
auto-save-done = Saved the commits of { $project } into { $repository } under refs/sbx/{ $namespace } first.
auto-save-failed = The commits of { $project } could not be saved into the host repository first, so anything committed since the last save is still only in the sandbox.
sync-done = Synced { $project } with { $repository }.
sync-unchanged = { $project } and { $repository } were already in sync.
sync-heading-host = Host repository
sync-heading-sandbox = Sandbox origin
sync-left-as-it-was = Git left the refs that were neither created nor updated as they were. Their commits are kept under refs/sbx/{ $namespace } in { $repository }.
sync-refused-because = Git refused { $reference }: { $reason }
sync-sandbox-untouched = The worktrees and branches in the sandbox were left as they were. To take the host's changes in, merge or rebase onto origin/<branch> inside the sandbox, then sync again to bring the result to the host.
files-secret-hint = Declared files carry configuration, not credentials. Keep tokens, secrets and private keys out of them and hand those to the sandbox with the secret feature of Docker Sandboxes instead.
apply-all-stopped-note = Stopped sandboxes were left as they were. Open a project to start its sandbox, then apply the files to it.
apply-files-done = { $count } declared files of { $project } were placed into { $sandbox }.
apply-worktrees-done = { $project } now has { $count } managed worktrees in { $sandbox }.
legend-attached = the worktree follows a branch that tracks the remote
legend-detached = the worktree sits on a commit without a branch
legend-managed = the project declares this worktree, and a rebuild recreates it
legend-unmanaged = the worktree was made inside the sandbox, and nothing recreates it
legend-pushed = the upstream branch was last observed to hold every commit here
legend-reachable = a ref of the origin, or one saved on the host, was last observed to reach this commit
legend-unreachable = no ref of the origin, and nothing saved on the host, was last observed to reach this commit
legend-unobservable = whether the remote reaches this commit could not be checked; the value shows the reason
legend-placed = the file was written into the sandbox
legend-ref-created = the ref was created
legend-ref-updated = the ref moved forward from its previous tip
legend-ref-replaced = the ref moved to a tip that does not contain the previous one; the previous tip is kept under archive
legend-ref-deleted = the ref no longer exists in the sandbox; its previous tip is kept under archive
legend-sent-created = the ref reached the sandbox for the first time
legend-sent-updated = the ref moved to the tip the host repository has
legend-sent-removed = the branch no longer exists in the host repository, so the sandbox's origin dropped it
legend-sent-refused = Git refused the update, so the sandbox kept its own; the reason is noted below
legend-reflect-created = the branch or tag was created in the host repository
legend-reflect-updated = the host branch moved forward to the sandbox's tip
legend-reflect-behind = the sandbox branch is only behind the host branch, so nothing is lost
legend-reflect-diverged = the host branch and the sandbox branch each have commits the other lacks
legend-reflect-checked-out = the branch is checked out in the host repository, so Git did not move it
legend-reflect-exists = a tag of this name already points elsewhere in the host repository
legend-reflect-refused = Git refused the update for the reason noted below
legend-unchanged = the sandbox already held the same content
legend-modified = the sandbox copy was changed after sbxm placed it

